&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Commerce is the global leader in licensed sports merchandise, operating a vertically integrated platform that designs, manufactures, and delivers officially licensed apparel, jerseys, headwear, and collectibles for major leagues, teams, and events worldwide. With more than 900 e-commerce sites and a global omnichannel presence across digital, in-venue, and retail, Fanatics Commerce reaches fans in over 180 countries and powers official fan experiences for many of the world&#39;s most iconic sports properties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Fanatics, we bring our BOLD Leadership Principles to life every day - building championship teams, obsessing over fans, acting with entrepreneurial speed, and delivering with a determined and relentless mindset.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Commerce is the global leader in licensed sports merchandise, operating a vertically integrated platform that designs, manufactures, and delivers officially licensed apparel, jerseys, headwear, and collectibles for major leagues, teams, and events worldwide. With more than 900 e-commerce sites and a global omnichannel presence across digital, in-venue, and retail, Fanatics Commerce reaches fans in over 180 countries and powers official fan experiences for many of the world&#39;s most iconic sports properties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Fanatics, we bring our BOLD Leadership Principles to life every day—building championship teams, obsessing over fans, acting with limitless entrepreneurial spirit, and delivering with a determined and relentless mindset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we continue to scale our global platform, the Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment will play a critical role in leading end-to-end customer fulfilment capability across the EU region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROLE OVERVIEW&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Vice President, Operations and based in France, the Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment is responsible for leading and directing customer fulfilment across the EU region, building capacity and capability through both owned and third-party operations to service all verticals. The role owns the development and execution of operational strategies that improve speed of delivery, reduce cost, and drive down defects across the full supply chain from first to final mile. The Head of Operations – EU Fulfilment delivers business and fan impact through BOLD leadership and execution excellence, leveraging data, automation, and AI-enabled insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HOW WILL YOU DRIVE IMPACT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success is measured by the ability to deliver results through BOLD capabilities and measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with business leaders and stakeholders across the UK and EU, operational leaders spanning supply chain, freight, fulfilment, and final mile, and local technical and functional teams to align operational plans with broader business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen the France-based operational partnership with internal stakeholders across the international Senior Leadership Team, influencing effectively within a regional, matrixed environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop high-performing teams with clear ownership across key partners, verticals, and locations, fostering a culture of collaboration, transparency, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate operational excellence standards into 3PL environments, embedding accountability and performance ownership across all third-party operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fan &amp;amp; Customer Impact&lt;/strong&gt; (Obsessed with Fans)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategies to improve customer and partner satisfaction through faster delivery, lower cost, and reduced defect rates across the EU region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational plans that support all verticals and locales, ensuring consistent service quality and fulfilment performance for fans across every channel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor performance, contracts, and service delivery to ensure all partners meet or exceed agreed service levels and customer experience standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the selection and onboarding of new providers to support the growth plans of verticals and locales within the EU region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Problem Solving&lt;/strong&gt; (Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate capital expenditure projects into tangible ROI and measurable service benefits, ensuring investment decisions are grounded in data and operational insight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement plans to improve speed to delivery while simultaneously reducing cost and defects, identifying synergies across the EU region to optimise performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a change leader and owner, driving continuous improvement across 3PL and internal operations through innovative thinking and structured execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/strong&gt; (Determined &amp;amp; Relentless Mindset)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operations forecast and plans end-to-end, ensuring alignment between operational capacity and business demand across all EU verticals and locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise the speed and cost of service across the region, balancing efficiency with service quality and partner commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational synergies across the EU region, identifying and realising efficiencies that benefit customers, partners, and the broader Fanatics Commerce business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; DIGITAL CAPABILITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a future-ready organization. This role is expected to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply AI and technology to improve efficiency, quality, and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data and digital tools to inform decisions and enhance performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate curiosity and adaptability in adopting new technologies and ways of working&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a culture of innovation and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CAPABILITIES &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE YOU BRING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of operational leadership experience within complex, multi-site or omni-channel organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing 3PLs, including SLA ownership, contract management, and performance governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the end-to-end supply chain, from first mile through to final mile delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record as a change leader, owning and driving transformation across operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communicator and influencer with the ability to operate in regional, matrixed stakeholder environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;France-based operational experience is essential, with the ability to lead on-the-ground operations from a France base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing operational plans that deliver measurable improvements in speed, cost, and quality across multiple verticals and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WORK LOCATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hybrid: The primary place of performance of this role is the Company&#39;s office located in Paris, France, subject to the Company&#39;s current hybrid work policy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Fanatics, we operate with a BOLD mindset - We Build Championship Teams, we’re Obsessed with Fans, we embrace a Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit, and we approach every challenge with a Determined and Relentless Mindset. If you’re ready to contribute to a dynamic, fast-paced environment that thrives on collaboration and growth, we want you to be part of our team.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;ABOUT THE TEAM&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics Commerce is a leading designer, manufacturer, and seller of licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods. It operates a vertically-integrated platform of digital and physical capabilities for leading sports leagues, teams, colleges, and associations globally – as well as its flagship site, &lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanatics.com&quot;&gt;www.fanatics.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics Commerce has a broad range of online, sports venue, and vertical apparel partnerships worldwide, including comprehensive partnerships with leading leagues, teams, colleges, and sports organizations across the world—including the NFL, NBA, MLB, NHL, MLS, Formula 1, and Australian Football League (AFL); the Dallas Cowboys, Golden State Warriors, Paris Saint-Germain, Chelsea FC, and Tokyo Giants; the University of Notre Dame, University of Alabama, and University of Texas; the International Olympic Committee (IOC), England Rugby, and the Union of European Football Associations (UEFA).&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;At Fanatics Commerce, we infuse our BOLD Leadership Principles in everything we do:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Build Championship Teams&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Obsessed with Fans&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Limitless Entrepreneurial Spirit&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;· Determined and Relentless Mindset&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a -----
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Sony Interactive Entertainment?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment isn’t just the Best Place to Play — it’s also the Best Place to Work. Sony Interactive Entertainment (SIE) is the company behind the PlayStation brand. As a subsidiary of Sony Group Corporation, we’re part of a proud legacy of innovation and excellence. SIE is a dynamic technology company, delivering cutting-edge hardware and network services to more than 100 million people and an entertainment leader, home to some of the most beloved and recognizable intellectual properties (IP) in the world. Our role at SIE is to create and nurture the experiences under the PlayStation brand, a name synonymous with entertainment excellence and creativity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of Finance Systems Engineering is a technology and engineering leader responsible for delivering and evolving systems that enable critical Finance capabilities. Reporting to a Senior Director in IT, this role will lead teams responsible for enterprise planning and forecasting platforms, custom-built Finance solutions, and SaaS applications that complement the core SAP ERP ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director will lead a multidisciplinary team that includes planning model builders, systems analysts/product owners/TPMs, and software engineering professionals. This leader will partner closely with Finance to translate business priorities and transformation objectives into scalable technology solutions that simplify processes, improve decision making, and enable greater use of data, automation, AI, and machine learning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A key responsibility of the role is strengthening the team’s ability to connect Finance domain expertise with specialized data and machine learning capabilities, enabling Finance to translate its AI and ML objectives into scalable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will combine strong engineering and people leadership with Finance domain knowledge and experience across enterprise planning platforms, custom software development, SaaS solutions, integration architectures, data, and AI/ML technologies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance Systems Leadership &amp;amp; Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multidisciplinary teams responsible for planning and forecasting platforms, custom Finance solutions, and Finance-related SaaS applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance leaders to understand business priorities and translate Finance transformation objectives into technology strategies, roadmaps, and solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technology portfolio and multi-year roadmap balancing business priorities, technical debt, platform lifecycle, and operational sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish engineering and product practices that balance speed, business value, user experience, scalability, reliability, security, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong partnerships with Enterprise Architecture, Data Engineering, ML Engineering, Integration, Infrastructure, Cybersecurity, and other technology teams to deliver cohesive end-to-end solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage strategic technology vendors and implementation partners to ensure successful delivery, operational excellence, and continuous innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop a high performing organization across model building, systems analysis/product ownership, and software engineering disciplines while fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, innovation, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning, Finance Applications &amp;amp; Software Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technology leadership for enterprise-scale financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and scenario-modeling solutions used across Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the engineering, maintenance, and support of custom applications and services that address Finance-specific business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide leadership for Finance SaaS applications adjacent to the core SAP ERP ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Finance solutions integrate effectively with SAP and the broader enterprise application and data ecosystem while maintaining appropriate architectural standards and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI, ML and Data Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance leaders to identify opportunities where data, AI, and machine learning can improve planning, forecasting, financial analysis, automation, and decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess capability gaps and establish development plans, role expectations, and ways of working that prepare the Finance Systems Engineering organization to collaborate effectively with Data Engineering and ML Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable teams to translate Finance business problems and domain knowledge into well-defined data, AI, and ML use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with specialized technology teams to incorporate enterprise data, predictive models, and AI/ML services into Finance applications and business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how Finance Systems Engineering will evaluate, adopt, and govern AI and ML capabilities available through enterprise applications, internal data and ML platforms, and approved external services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive adoption and operationalization of AI/ML capabilities within Finance while ensuring alignment with enterprise architecture, data governance, security, privacy, and technology standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Engineering, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of progressive experience leading enterprise application or software engineering organizations in a large enterprise environment, including accountability for multidisciplinary teams, technology delivery, and operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading through managers, including responsibility for organizational design, talent development, performance management, and succession planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building and leading multidisciplinary teams across software engineering, enterprise applications, planning applications, systems analysis, product ownership, and technical program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading enterprise scale financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and scenario-modeling platforms, including responsibility for platform strategy, delivery, lifecycle management, and operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Finance processes, particularly financial planning, budgeting, forecasting, and related Finance operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to partner with senior business leaders, translate business and transformation objectives into technology strategy and execution, and own multi-year portfolio roadmaps that balance business priorities, technical debt, platform lifecycle, and operational sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software engineering, enterprise architecture, integration, data, and cloud concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to develop technical talent and build new capabilities within an engineering organization, including preparing teams to partner effectively with Data Engineering and ML Engineering and to operationalize data, AI, and machine learning capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication, stakeholder management, and cross functional leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with one or more enterprise-scale planning and forecasting platforms, such as Anaplan, Workday Adaptive Planning, or SAP Analytics Cloud, including solution design, model governance, integration, or platform administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading software engineering teams building custom enterprise solutions using Golang, Java or comparable programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with event-driven and streaming architectures and enterprise integration patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a portfolio of Finance SaaS solutions, such as Coupa, Rightsline, or comparable platforms, including vendor management, integration, lifecycle planning, and operational governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SAP S/4HANA and integration of Finance applications and services with the core ERP environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in jointly delivering production AI or machine learning capabilities with Data Engineering and ML Engineering teams, including integration into enterprise applications or business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how AI and machine learning can be applied responsibly to Finance use cases, including forecasting, predictive insights, anomaly detection, decision support, and process automation, with attention to data governance, security, privacy, and enterprise technology standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting technology enabled Finance transformation within a large, global organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please note, Sony Interactive Entertainment conducts background checks at the offer stage for all new employees (which may include criminal background checks for some roles) and will need to process personal information to support these checks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Please refer to our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.playstation.com/legal/careers-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;for more information about what personal information we collect, how we use it, who we share it with, and your data protection rights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All persons will receive consideration for employment without regard to gender (including gender identity, gender expression and gender reassignment), race (including colour, nationality, ethnic or national origin), religion or belief, marital or civil partnership status, disability, age, sexual orientation, pregnancy, maternity or parental status, trade union membership or membership in any other legally protected category.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;We strive to create an inclusive environment, empower employees and embrace diversity. We encourage everyone to respond.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Sony Interactive Entertainment is a Fair Chance employer and qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records will be considered for employment.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 110, 153);&quot;&gt;What Cognite is:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 41, 255);&quot;&gt;Relentless&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(102, 110, 153);&quot;&gt;to achieve&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Cognite operates at the forefront of &lt;strong&gt;industrial digitalization, building AI&lt;/strong&gt;, and data solutions that solve the world’s hardest, highest-impact problems. With unmatched industrial heritage and a comprehensive suite of AI capabilities, including low-code AI agents, Cognite accelerates the digital transformation to drive operational improvements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We thrive in challenges. We challenge assumptions. We execute with speed and ownership. If you view obstacles as signals to step forward - not backwards - you’ll feel right at home here.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.cognite.com/en/company/newsroom/cognite-s-industrial-ai-momentum-soars-driving-ecosystem-impact-at-global-conference&quot;&gt;Moonshot&lt;/a&gt; is bold: Unlock $100B in customer value by 2035, and redefine how global industry works. Join us in this venture where AI and data meet ingenuity, and together, we will forge the path to a smarter, more connected industrial future.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;img style=&quot;display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 100%;&quot; width=&quot;708&quot;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Field / Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel:&lt;/strong&gt; Approximately 50% (Client sites, etc)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Cognite&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cognite is a global industrial Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) company enabling the full-scale digital transformation of heavy-asset industries. Our core software product, Cognite Data Fusion (CDF), powers companies with contextualized OT/IT data to develop and scale solutions that increase safety, sustainability, and operational efficiency while driving revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Business Development Director within our Supply Chain Center of Excellence (CoE)&lt;/strong&gt;, you will drive Cognite’s growth by winning new Supply Chain business within accounts headquartered in your territory. Operating as a subject matter expert, you will leverage deep domain insights to help customers transform their supply chain value chain using Cognite Applications and the Cognite Data Fusion Platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Territory &amp;amp; CoE Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and execute a targeted territory strategy to accelerate bookings growth and secure high-impact supply chain clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Generation:&lt;/strong&gt; Actively prospect and leverage your personal network to generate pipeline, providing compelling &quot;commercial insights&quot; on optimizing the supply chain value chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Complex Sales Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead extended territory teams (including pre-sales and technical experts) through complex enterprise sales cycles to exceed bookings targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value-Based Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Quantify ROI and present strong business cases to help enterprise executives justify software investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner-savvy:&lt;/strong&gt; work with partners to qualify and progress their pipeline, and drive joint engagements on qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal Negotiation:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account / Engagement Leader in negotiating favorable pricing and commercial terms with C-level executives by demonstrating the long-term strategic value of Cognite’s solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with internal Product Management and Marketing teams to feed real-market supply chain insights back into product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Hygiene &amp;amp; Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Support the Account Leaders and their First Line Managers in accurately forecasting monthly/quarterly bookings and maintaining up-to-date account records in &lt;a href=&quot;http://salesforce.com&quot;&gt;Salesforce.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge, Skills, Abilities (KSAs) &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Domain &amp;amp; Industry Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Deep domain expertise in complex Supply Chain operations for Energy, Manufacturing or Power Utilities verticals. Understanding of Production operations and industry x.0 initiatives is also required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Value Selling:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to sell value and build quantified ROI frameworks for prospective buyers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Informal Leadership, Influence &amp;amp; Autonomy:&lt;/strong&gt; High degree of self-motivation, time management, and ability to informally lead and effectively influence cross-functional deal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Stellar presentation, written, and verbal communication skills tailored for C-suite engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; Technical Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Software/SaaS:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven mastery of selling complex analytics or data platforms (e.g., AI, Big Data, Data Warehousing, Business Intelligence, Machine Learning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Ecosystems:&lt;/strong&gt; Familiarity with modern data architectures and tools, such as Big Data frameworks (Hadoop, Spark, Hive, BigQuery), Data Warehouses, and Machine Learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 10+ years of experience in the Manufacturing and broader industrial supply chain environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Track Record:&lt;/strong&gt; 7+ years of direct or in-support sales experience, selling enterprise software/SaaS (BI, Big Data, Advanced Analytics, or AI/ML) to C-level executives, Management and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Performance:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated history of consistently meeting or exceeding SaaS bookings goals in direct / partner / channel-based sales models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Prior experience operating in high-growth startup environments (Series A, B, or C stage).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor’s degree required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes Us Great &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture &amp;amp; Values:&lt;/strong&gt; High autonomy, a culture of speed and openness, social and diversity initiatives (Together@Cognite), and a commitment to innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive base + variable compensation, 401(k) employer matching, fully covered health/dental/vision/disability premiums, and learning stipends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workplace Flexibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Unlimited PTO, paid parental leave, and catered company lunches.&lt;/li&gt;
